Hardware bug: when two multiply/divide instructions are adjacent (div then rem, rem then div, divu then remu), the second one returns the first one's result. rv32im_pipeline_core.vhd raises the start of a multiply/divide only on the rising edge of "the instruction in ID is a multiply/divide" (startMul_raw = cu_isMulDiv and not isMulDiv_d), so the second operation of a pair never starts. Found with GHDL on the real hardware top and confirmed correct on Spike: 42 / 10 and 42 % 10 give 4 and 4 instead of 4 and 2. Turn this on once the core starts every operation.
